Date: Wed, 26 Jan 2022 09:14:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: intel: fix wrong register name in intel_shim_wake

When clearing the sdw wakests status, we should use SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS.

Fixes: 4a17c441c7cb ("soundwire: intel: revisit SHIM programming sequences.")
Signed-off-by: Libin Yang <libin.yang@intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Pierre-Louis Bossart <pierre-louis.bossart@linux.intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Rander Wang <rander.wang@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Bard Liao <yung-chuan.liao@linux.intel.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20220126011451.27853-1-yung-chuan.liao@linux.intel.com
Signed-off-by: Vinod Koul <vkoul@kernel.org>

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/intel.c b/drivers/soundwire/intel.c
index 122f7a29d8ca..63101f1ba271 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/intel.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/intel.c
@@ -448,8 +448,8 @@ static void intel_shim_wake(struct sdw_intel *sdw, bool wake_enable)

 		/* Clear wake status */
 		wake_sts = intel_readw(shim, SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS);
-		wake_sts |= (SDW_SHIM_WAKEEN_ENABLE << link_id);
-		intel_writew(shim, SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS_STATUS, wake_sts);
+		wake_sts |= (SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS_STATUS << link_id);
+		intel_writew(shim, SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS, wake_sts);
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(sdw->link_res->shim_lock);
 }
-- 
2.25.1

### Modifications in Each File

1. **File: `drivers/soundwire/intel.c`**
   - The line that clears the wake status has been modified:
     - **Original Code:**
       ```c
       wake_sts = intel_readw(shim, SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS);
       wake_sts |= (SDW_SHIM_WAKEEN_ENABLE << link_id);
       intel_writew(shim, SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS_STATUS, wake_sts);
       ```
     - **Modified Code:**
       ```c
       wake_sts = intel_readw(shim, SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS);
       wake_sts |= (SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS_STATUS << link_id);
       intel_writew(shim, SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS, wake_sts);
       ```

### Relationships Between Modifications

- The patch corrects the use of the register name in the `intel_shim_wake` function. Specifically, it changes the register used for writing the wake status from `SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS_STATUS` to `SDW_SHIM_WAKESTS`. This change ensures that the correct register is accessed when clearing the wake status, addressing a bug introduced in a previous commit (4a17c441c7cb). The modification is crucial for the proper functioning of the SoundWire interface in Intel hardware.

